        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sl",
          "text": "Pain and suffering cover physical discomfort, emotional distress, and loss of enjoyment, not just medical bills.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1so",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sn",
          "text": "Two main methods determine the value: the Multiplier Method for serious injuries and the Per Diem Method for shorter recoveries.c",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1sq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sp",
          "text": "Colorado raised its noneconomic damages cap to $1.5 million for claims filed on or after January 1, 2025.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1ss",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sr",
          "text": "Several factors shape the final number, including injury severity, recovery length, quality of life impact, and fault percentage.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1su",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1st",
          "text": "Documentation matters. A pain journal strengthens a claim by giving attorneys concrete, hard-to-dispute evidence.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1t1",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l1sw",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/do-i-have-to-pay-medical-bills-out-of-my-settlement/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sv",
          "text": "Most people injured in a Denver accident know they can seek ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sx",
          "text": "compensation for medical bills",
          "marks": [
            "l1sw"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sy",
          "text": " and lost wages, but the losses that never appear on a receipt, the pain, the fear, the disruption to daily life, often add up to far more. ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1sz",
          "text": "“How is pain and suffering calculated?”",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1t0",
          "text": " is one of the most common questions injured Coloradans ask, and the answer matters because noneconomic damages frequently represent the largest portion of a personal injury award.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1t8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l1t5",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1t2",
          "text": "At ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1t3",
          "text": "Dormer Harpring",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1t4",
          "text": ", our ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1t6",
          "text": "personal injury lawyers",
          "marks": [
            "l1t5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1t7",
          "text": " understand how disorienting the period after an accident can be, and we guide injured Coloradans through every step of the process so they never have to face an insurer’s tactics alone or unprepared.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1ta",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1t9",
          "text": "Under What Circumstances Can You Expect Compensation for Pain and Suffering?",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1tf",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l1tc",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/contributory-negligence-vs-comparative-negligence/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tb",
          "text": "Colorado personal injury law entitles injured individuals to seek non-economic damages when another party’s ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1td",
          "text": "negligence",
          "marks": [
            "l1tc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1te",
          "text": " caused their harm. These damages address what the injury has taken from everyday life, going well beyond bills and missed paychecks.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1tk",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l1th",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/pain_and_suffering"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tg",
          "text": "The term",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ti",
          "text": " pain and suffering",
          "marks": [
            "l1th"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tj",
          "text": " refers to the physical discomfort and emotional distress compensable as non-economic damages, encompassing the anguish, inconvenience, and emotional trauma accompanying an injury. Common circumstances where this compensation applies include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1tn",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tl",
          "text": "Physical pain:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tm",
          "text": " Ongoing discomfort, chronic pain, or permanent physical limitations resulting from the injury.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1tq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1to",
          "text": "Emotional distress:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tp",
          "text": " Anxiety, depression, PTSD, or mood disruptions directly connected to the accident.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1tt",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tr",
          "text": "Loss of enjoyment:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ts",
          "text": " An inability to participate in hobbies, exercise, or family activities that the injury has interrupted.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1tw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tu",
          "text": "Sleep disruption:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tv",
          "text": " Persistent insomnia or recurring nightmares tied to the trauma of the accident.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1tz",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1tx",
          "text": "Loss of consortium:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ty",
          "text": " The impact on a spouse or close family member’s relationship with the injured person.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1u1",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1u0",
          "text": "Keeping a personal journal of daily symptoms from day one can meaningfully strengthen a claim down the road, giving your attorney a clearer, more complete picture of how the injury has affected your life.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "image",
      "_key": "i1u2",
      "src": "./images/2026-04-how-is-pain-and-suffering-calculated.jpg",
      "alt": "how is pain and suffering calculated"
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1u4",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1u3",
          "text": "Popular Calculation Methods",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1u6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1u5",
          "text": "In Denver, Colorado, two primary methods are widely used by insurance companies and attorneys to calculate pain and suffering in personal injury cases: the Multiplier Method and the Per Diem Method.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1u8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1u7",
          "text": "Both assign a monetary value to subjective losses such as physical pain, mental anguish, emotional distress, and loss of enjoyment of life, giving attorneys and insurers a working framework for negotiating non-economic damages.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1ua",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1u9",
          "text": "The Multiplier Method",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1ue",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ub",
          "text": "The multiplier method serves as the most common approach for serious or long-term injuries. When asking ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uc",
          "text": "“How is pain and suffering calculated?”",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ud",
          "text": " under this formula, the process starts by totaling all economic damages, including medical expenses, lost wages, and property damage, then multiplying that total by a number generally ranging from 1.5 to 5, depending on injury severity:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1uh",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uf",
          "text": "1.5x to 2x:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ug",
          "text": " Minor injuries with short recovery times.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1uk",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ui",
          "text": "3x:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uj",
          "text": " Moderate injuries involving significant pain and a lengthy recovery.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1un",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ul",
          "text": "4x to 5x or higher:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1um",
          "text": " Severe, permanent, or life-altering injuries.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1up",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uo",
          "text": "If medical bills and lost wages total $20,000 and a multiplier of 3 applies, the pain and suffering component reaches $60,000, bringing the total claim value to $80,000. What moves that multiplier up or down in Colorado includes injury permanence, strength of medical documentation, clarity of liability, and how persuasively an attorney presents the full picture at the negotiating table or before a jury.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1ur",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uq",
          "text": "Consistent medical treatment matters more than most people expect. Gaps in treatment give insurers grounds to argue that the injury was not as serious as claimed, which can significantly reduce the multiplier.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1ut",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1us",
          "text": "The Per Diem Method",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1uv",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uu",
          "text": "The per diem method assigns a specific dollar value to each day of suffering, from the accident date through the point of Maximum Medical Improvement, where a treating physician determines the patient has recovered as fully as medicine allows. This approach works best for shorter-term injuries with a clearly defined recovery period, and the daily rate often reflects the injured person’s daily income on the rationale that enduring pain deserves at least the same value as a day’s work.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1ux",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uw",
          "text": "If a daily rate of $200 applies over a 100-day recovery, the pain and suffering award reaches $20,000. In some cases, attorneys present both the multiplier and per diem calculations during negotiations to demonstrate the full range of what a claim reasonably supports.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1uz",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1uy",
          "text": "Other Methods",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1v1",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1v0",
          "text": "Insurance companies sometimes rely on proprietary software algorithms, such as Colossus, to generate settlement offers. These tools are built to favor the insurer and routinely produce figures that bear little relationship to what a case actually warrants, so treating that output as a starting point rather than a final number is worth keeping in mind.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1v3",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1v2",
          "text": "Attorneys counter this by studying jury precedents from comparable Colorado cases to build a more grounded framework for what a judge or jury might reasonably award. Negotiation ultimately resolves most claims before trial, but having an attorney who understands both the data and the courtroom puts an injured person in a much stronger position.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1v5",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1v4",
          "text": "Factors That Go Into a Pain and Suffering Calculation",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1va",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l1v7",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/how-much-is-my-personal-injury-case-worth/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1v6",
          "text": "Multiple variables shift the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1v8",
          "text": "final value of a claim",
          "marks": [
            "l1v7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1v9",
          "text": ", and knowing which ones carry the most weight helps explain why two seemingly similar cases can produce very different outcomes.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1vh",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l1vc",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/hb24-1472"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vb",
          "text": "Under",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vd",
          "text": " HB24-1472",
          "marks": [
            "l1vc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1ve",
          "text": ", for civil actions filed on or after January 1, 2025, Colorado raised the cap on noneconomic damages from $250,000 to $1.5 million, with inflation-based adjustments beginning January 1, 2028, representing a significant shift in ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vf",
          "text": "“How is pain and suffering calculated?”",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vg",
          "text": " for higher-value claims across the state. Key factors attorneys and insurers weigh include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1vn",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l1vk",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/catastrophic-personal-injury/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vi",
          "text": "Injury severity:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vj",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vl",
          "text": "Catastrophic injuries",
          "marks": [
            "l1vk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vm",
          "text": " such as traumatic brain injuries or spinal cord damage command higher non-economic awards.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1vq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vo",
          "text": "Recovery duration:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vp",
          "text": " A years-long or permanent recovery compounds damages considerably under both primary calculation methods.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1vt",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vr",
          "text": "Quality of life impact:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vs",
          "text": " How the injury altered the plaintiff’s ability to work, connect with family, and engage in everyday activities carries significant weight with juries and adjusters alike.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1vw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vu",
          "text": "Expert testimony:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vv",
          "text": " Medical professionals and occupational therapists provide third-party validation of ongoing limitations, lending credibility that insurers find harder to dismiss.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b1vz",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vx",
          "text": "Colorado’s comparative fault rule:",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s1vy",
          "text": " Under Colorado’s modified comparative fault standard, compensation reduces proportionally by the injured party’s percentage of fault, and a finding of 50% or greater fault bars recovery entirely.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
